#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Attaches the delegation note to the start of every session.
set -euo pipefail

cat <<'JSON'
{"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"SessionStart","additionalContext":"Shared assistants are available and should be used by default for volume work:\n\n- finder: locate files, docs, tickets, or records\n- researcher: read external documentation and report back\n- builder: complete a scoped piece of work once direction is settled\n- analyst: spreadsheets, data pulls, and reducing long output\n- checker: independently verify finished work before you report done\n\nHand off work whose cost is reading or producing a lot of material. Keep planning, integration, and the final call here.\n\nWhen a project has independent pieces, dispatch builders in parallel in a single message rather than one at a time. That is what lets a multi-part project finish in one session.\n\nDo not hand off work you could finish yourself in a few steps; each handoff costs a fresh context plus a report to read back.\n\nAssistants proceed on stated assumptions rather than stopping to ask, so read the assumptions in their reports before integrating.\n\nYou own completion. They finish their pieces; you finish the project. Do not report done until every part is done, and use checker to confirm rather than trusting your own summary."}}
JSON
